  "seoBody": "<h2>How much does Fluix cost?</h2><p>Fluix publishes Crews at 29 US dollars per user a month with a minimum of five users, and Operations at 49 US dollars per user a month with a minimum of fifteen users. Enterprise is custom pricing with a minimum of twenty-five. Those minimums are the part that catches smaller firms out: a team with three inspectors still buys five licences on the entry plan.</p><h2>Why look for a Fluix alternative?</h2><p>Usually size, not quality. Fluix is built for large field operations with formal approval chains, and it does that well. A UK firm with a handful of inspectors is buying a block of seats it does not need, in an app each worker has to install and log into.</p><h2>What does Quickler do differently?</h2><p>Checks arrive in the WhatsApp or Telegram already on the worker's phone, so there is nothing to install and no login. The finished record is written into your own report template, the Word or PDF your firm already issues, with your styles, headings, tables and logo kept. Pricing is £75 per phone number a month, where a phone number counts when it did at least one check that month, so people who do nothing that month cost nothing.</p><h2>What is Fluix better at?</h2><p>Formal multi-stage approvals with e-signature, offline capture inside the app, scheduling and asset records, and published SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001 certification. If a client's procurement team requires documented approval chains or those certifications, Fluix answers that directly and we would say so.</p>",
